# A host node_modules is the wrong platform's binaries and megabytes of context;
# the ui stage runs its own npm ci.
web/node_modules
web/.tanstack
# The bundle is a BUILD OUTPUT. The ui stage builds it fresh and the go stage
# takes it with COPY --from=ui, so this line is about what the CONTEXT must not
# smuggle in.
#
# It matters because COPY merges a directory rather than replacing it —
# MEASURED, not assumed: with a stale dist/OLD-HASH.js in the context and a
# fresh dist/NEW-HASH.js in the source stage, the image ends up holding BOTH,
# while index.html is overwritten by the fresh one. A developer's stale local
# dist would therefore leave orphaned hashed assets nothing references sitting
# in every image built on that machine, and vite's emptyOutDir — which does
# prune — would never get the chance to clean them, because it ran in a
# different stage.
backend/internal/webui/dist
